{#- Self-hosted webfonts, site artefacts only (phase 0R, T1).

    0j (W0-6) banned webfonts and this does not overturn that — it scopes it.
    The ban had two reasons and neither reaches the site:

      * `preview.html` is *defined* by being one self-contained file. A font
        reference would make it two files, so it keeps the stack alone.
      * `email.html` is stripped of `@font-face` by every mail client worth
        naming, so shipping one would be weight with no effect.

    The site is neither. These are **same-origin files at a relative path**, so
    "the whole site fetches nothing" is still true — the check for it now looks
    for `url(http` rather than for the string `@font-face`, which is the
    property it was always trying to assert.

    Latin subset only, and Source Serif 4 and Public Sans are variable, so one
    file covers 400–700. Total 240 KB across six files. The **Korean stack has
    no webfont**: Hangul subsets are an order of magnitude larger and /ko/ is
    phase 1, so it keeps falling back to whatever the reader has.

    `font-display: swap` throughout: the text is the product, and a reader
    should never wait on a typeface to read a headline. -#}

@font-face {
  font-family: "Source Serif 4";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400 700;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url("{{ font_prefix }}source-serif-4-400.woff2") format("woff2");
}
@font-face {
  font-family: "Source Serif 4";
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 400 700;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url("{{ font_prefix }}source-serif-4-400-italic.woff2") format("woff2");
}
@font-face {
  font-family: "Public Sans";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400 700;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url("{{ font_prefix }}public-sans-400.woff2") format("woff2");
}
@font-face {
  font-family: "Public Sans";
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 400 700;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url("{{ font_prefix }}public-sans-400-italic.woff2") format("woff2");
}
{#- IBM Plex Mono is **not** variable: 400 and 600 are separate files, and
    naming them after the family alone made the second silently overwrite the
    first while the vendoring script reported both. -#}
@font-face {
  font-family: "IBM Plex Mono";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url("{{ font_prefix }}ibm-plex-mono-400.woff2") format("woff2");
}
@font-face {
  font-family: "IBM Plex Mono";
  font-style: normal;
  font-weight: 600;
  font-display: swap;
  src: url("{{ font_prefix }}ibm-plex-mono-600.woff2") format("woff2");
}
